# N2b evidence: a waiting voice offer hears only yes or no, and expires
# written 2026-11-04T18:21:33Z on 4338c1c plus the uncommitted N2b code; Python 3.13.18
# Scratch folder (not committed): S=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-surya-OS-local-ai/a2d9d327-0aab-56b9-8f14-a234bbf8ed79/scratchpad/n2b. Router: NOVA's own command model. No microphone: the listener prints lines.

## 1. Overheard speech while an offer waits (confirm_seconds = 30)
$ cat $S/room/overheard.py
print("nova remember that the gate code is 4321", flush=True)
print("my friend said CANARY-ROOM-TALK-12 just now", flush=True)
print("Yes.", flush=True)
[exit 0]

$ rm -rf $S/overheard/state; PYTHONPATH=novacore/src python3 -m novacore --config $S/overheard/config.toml --voice
[voice] listening. Say "Nova" and a command.
nova> NOVA would save this note: "the gate code is 4321" (memory.save). Type yes to do it, or no to cancel.
nova> Saved note 2b74b49a-9a4d-4392-a28c-3982ef4199c9.
[voice] the listener stopped (status 0).
[exit 0]

$ wc -l < $S/overheard/state/memories.jsonl; grep -rl CANARY-ROOM-TALK-12 $S/overheard || echo 'canary in no file under the run folder'
1
canary in no file under the run folder
[exit 0]

## 2. An offer left waiting (confirm_seconds = 1; the listener waits 4 s)
$ cat $S/room/late.py
import time
print("nova remember that the gate code is 4321", flush=True)
time.sleep(4)
print("yes", flush=True)
print("nova yes", flush=True)
[exit 0]

$ rm -rf $S/late/state; PYTHONPATH=novacore/src python3 -m novacore --config $S/late/config.toml --voice
[voice] listening. Say "Nova" and a command.
nova> NOVA would save this note: "the gate code is 4321" (memory.save). Type yes to do it, or no to cancel.
[voice] the offer waited more than 1 s for yes or no; it expired and nothing was done.
nova> I am NovaCore, running strictly local via CLI.
[voice] the listener stopped (status 0).
[exit 0]

$ ls $S/late/state; test -e $S/late/state/memories.jsonl && echo 'a note was saved' || echo 'no note saved'
router
no note saved
[exit 0]

